.claude
issues.md
gui(abandoned)
webgui(abandoned)
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ─── userdata\ — settings, messages and logs ──────────────────────────────────
# Everything the user or this machine owns now lives in one folder, so this is
# one rule instead of the six scattered ones v1 had. It also closes a real leak:
# mass_gui.cfg used to be TRACKED, which put the maintainer's model names,
# calibrated OCR rects and DefaultFu3 message body into every clone.
#
# NOTE THE  /*  — without it the negation below is dead. Git never descends into
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so "userdata/" + "!userdata/hotkeys.default.ini" would
# silently stop tracking the default, and nobody would notice until a fresh clone
# had no keys to seed from. Excluding the CONTENTS is what makes !… reachable.
userdata/*
!userdata/hotkeys.default.ini

# ─── other people's data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS REMOTE IS PUBLIC. Everything below contains other people's data: fan
# display names, their messages, and purchase amounts. Screenshots of the live
# Infloww UI in particular show real handles in the tab strip and chat. The code
# needs none of it at runtime — only slice_elements.py and `automation.py --image`
# read these, and both are pointed at a file by hand.
#
# The listener itself is NOT in here: it is runtime, so it lives in
# src/services/automation/ and is tracked. Only the screenshots and the one-off
# detector prototypes stay out.
tools/ui-research/

# Screenshots automation.py drops while debugging a miss. Live UI, so same rule.
# The code recreates the folder on demand.
src/services/automation/debug/

# The packaged installer — a build output, rebuilt by tools/installer/build.bat.
tools/installer/dist/

# ─── debuglogs\ — diagnostics ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crash traces and probe dumps. Throwaway by nature, and they contain live UI
# text: the next-follow-up probe writes back the whole conversation it OCR'd, so
# this is fan messages on disk and must never reach a public remote. paths.ahk
# recreates the folder on demand, so nothing here needs tracking.
debuglogs/

# A log that should never have existed, twice. automation.py resolved MMA_LOG one
# folder short of the repo root, so instead of appending to the shared log it
# created a second one HERE — and that one was tracked, so every run of the
# listener showed up as a commit-able change. That was fixed, but the file kept
# coming back, because pinger.pyw had the SAME bug and nobody had looked at it:
# it climbed two levels instead of four while its own docstring promised "MMA's
# error_log.txt". Both now write to debuglogs\. This entry stays in case an old
# copy of either script is still running somewhere.
src/services/error_log.txt
